      "data": {
        "title": "Twilite as a native application, not a page running in someone else’s browser",
        "description": "A native (non-browser) Twilite — something like an Electron-style shell or a native webview host — that renders pages itself, rather than asking a third-party page to allow being framed by an ordinary browser tab.",
        "differentiator": "Does not depend on the target page cooperating (sidesteps the X-Frame-Options / CSP problem entirely) and is not boxed in by what a same-origin iframe is allowed to do.",
        "definitionKey": "idea-proposed-approach",
