      "data": {
        "view": {
          "intent": "node",
          "payload": "node.web.detail"
        },
        "semanticLevel": "detail",
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# A Non-Browser Twilite\n\nA brainstorm, not a decision: could Twilite run outside a browser — a native shell with its own page-rendering engine — so an actual web page can be a real, working graph node, instead of an iframe that most sites refuse to allow and that never quite behaves like a native node even when it does?\n\nThis graph exists to start that conversation. The problem, audience, and approach recorded here are a first honest guess at *why* this matters, reasoning forward from one line Michael gave: \"a non-browser based version of Twilite so we can render pages as nodes properly.\" None of it is confirmed yet."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "ownsContent": true,
          "surfaceDelegation": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "non-browser-twilite"
        }
      }
    },
